    "['ssh server compatibility enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh protocol-version v2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services ssh protocol-version v2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\nset system services ssh ciphers aes128-ctr aes192-ctr aes256-ctr\\n##\\n\\nNote: While Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 command for \"ssh server compatibility enable\" (which in Huawei enables compatibility with older SSH clients), the equivalent functionality in Juniper is achieved by:\\n1. Explicitly setting SSH protocol version to v2 (which is secure and widely compatible)\\n2. Configuring compatible cipher suites (matching the Huawei configuration)\\n3. SSH service is enabled by default in Juniper\\n\\nThe Huawei command essentially ensures backward compatibility, which in Juniper is handled by proper protocol and cipher configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh protocol-version v2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh ciphers aes128-ctr aes192-ctr aes256-ctr', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services ssh ciphers aes128-ctr aes192-ctr aes256-ctr', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system services ssh protocol-version v2\\nset system services ssh ciphers aes128-ctr aes192-ctr aes256-ctr\\n##\\n\\nNote: While Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact 1:1 command for \"ssh server compatibility enable\" (which in Huawei enables compatibility with older SSH clients), the equivalent functionality in Juniper is achieved by:\\n1. Explicitly setting SSH protocol version to v2 (which is secure and widely compatible)\\n2. Configuring compatible cipher suites (matching the Huawei configuration)\\n3. SSH service is enabled by default in Juniper\\n\\nThe Huawei command essentially ensures backward compatibility, which in Juniper is handled by proper protocol and cipher configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh ciphers aes128-ctr aes192-ctr aes256-ctr'}]]": 1,
