    "['local-user [parameter1] password irreversible-cipher [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"$5$UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC\"\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses `class super-user` to approximate privilege level 15\\n2. The encrypted password format differs between vendors, so I\\'ve represented it with a generic encrypted format indicator (the actual encrypted string would need to be compatible with JunOS)\\n3. The service-type ssh is implied by the login user configuration in Juniper\\n4. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"irreversible-cipher\" concept, but uses encrypted passwords stored with hashing algorithms', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"$5$UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC\"', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"$5$UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC\"', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"$5$UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC\"\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses `class super-user` to approximate privilege level 15\\n2. The encrypted password format differs between vendors, so I\\'ve represented it with a generic encrypted format indicator (the actual encrypted string would need to be compatible with JunOS)\\n3. The service-type ssh is implied by the login user configuration in Juniper\\n4. Juniper doesn\\'t have the exact \"irreversible-cipher\" concept, but uses encrypted passwords stored with hashing algorithms', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 authentication encrypted-password \"$5$UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC\"'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] privilege level [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI command `local-user client001 privilege level 15`:\\n\\n##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `super-user` is equivalent to privilege level 15 (highest privileges)\\n- The command creates/updates a user named \"client001\" with super-user privileges\\n- This matches the functionality of the HUAWEI command which sets the local user\\'s privilege level to the maximum (15)', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}]]": 1,
    "['local-user [parameter1] service-type ssh', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `local-user client001 service-type ssh` in Huawei configures the user \"client001\" to have SSH access. \\n2. In Juniper:\\n   - The first command sets the user class to \"super-user\" (equivalent to privilege level 15 in Huawei)\\n   - The second command enables SSH services (implied by the service-type ssh in Huawei)\\n3. The password configuration would be separate in Juniper, but wasn\\'t part of the requested translation.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services ssh', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `local-user client001 service-type ssh` in Huawei configures the user \"client001\" to have SSH access. \\n2. In Juniper:\\n   - The first command sets the user class to \"super-user\" (equivalent to privilege level 15 in Huawei)\\n   - The second command enables SSH services (implied by the service-type ssh in Huawei)\\n3. The password configuration would be separate in Juniper, but wasn\\'t part of the requested translation.', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh'}]]": 1,
