    "['authentication-mode aaa', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"', 'parent_command': ['set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Juniper equivalent involves multiple commands to achieve the same functionality as the Huawei `authentication-mode aaa` in VTY lines.\\n2. The commands:\\n   - Create the user with password (equivalent to AAA local-user)\\n   - Set privilege level (super-user = level 15)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n3. In Juniper, there\\'s no direct VTY line configuration like Huawei - these settings are system-wide for all access methods.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system login user client001 class super-user', 'parent_command': ['set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Juniper equivalent involves multiple commands to achieve the same functionality as the Huawei `authentication-mode aaa` in VTY lines.\\n2. The commands:\\n   - Create the user with password (equivalent to AAA local-user)\\n   - Set privilege level (super-user = level 15)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n3. In Juniper, there\\'s no direct VTY line configuration like Huawei - these settings are system-wide for all access methods.', 'trans_template': 'set system login user client001 class super-user'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password', 'parent_command': ['set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system services ssh connection-limit [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset system login user client001 authentication plain-text-password \"@%@%UyQs4,KTtSwJo(4QmW#K,LC:@%@%\"\\nset system login user client001 class super-user\\nset system services ssh authentication-order password\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The Juniper equivalent involves multiple commands to achieve the same functionality as the Huawei `authentication-mode aaa` in VTY lines.\\n2. The commands:\\n   - Create the user with password (equivalent to AAA local-user)\\n   - Set privilege level (super-user = level 15)\\n   - Configure SSH to use password authentication\\n3. In Juniper, there\\'s no direct VTY line configuration like Huawei - these settings are system-wide for all access methods.', 'trans_template': 'set system services ssh authentication-order password'}]]": 1,
